  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I understand. Cold food after that long a wait is disappointing. The $15 credit is the most I can give for a late delivery, and I can't add anything more for order #8101.\n\n**Pad thai from Lotus Garden (#8102):** I've refunded **$13.50** to your Visa ending in 4242. It should show up in 3\u20135 business days.\n\nUsually you could choose between a card refund of the item's price or account credit worth 20% more ($16.20). But there's a $25 limit on credit I can add in one conversation. With tonight's $15 credit, $16.20 more would put you over that limit. That's why the pad thai went back to your card.\n\nSo, to sum up:\n- **$15.00 account credit** for the late Saffron Lane order (ready to use now)\n- **$13.50 refund** to your Visa for the missing pad thai (3\u20135 business days)\n\nIs there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, I get that the credit is capped. The pad thai refund to my Visa works for me, I'd just rather have the money back on the card than wait on account credit anyway. Thanks for sorting both out."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I'm glad the card refund works for you. To recap:\n\n- **$15.00 account credit** for the late Saffron Lane order. It's on your account now and will be ready at checkout next time.\n- **$13.50 refund** to your Visa ending in 4242 for the missing pad thai. It should arrive in 3\u20135 business days.\n\nI'm sorry again about the late dinner and the missing pad thai. Enjoy your weekend, Maya!"
  }
